#!/bin/dmell
#
# icmp-start.dme - loads *and enables* the dmicmp module, which registers
# itself with dmip as the ICMPv4/ICMPv6 protocol handler from its own
# dmod_init() (see ../src/dmicmp.c). Once enabled, this device answers ICMP
# Echo Requests (ping) automatically, with no further setup needed. Run
# standalone (e.g. `dmell icmp-start.dme`) or as icmp.ini's exec, to bring it
# up at boot - see ../docs/service.md.
#
# Both steps are needed and they are not the same thing. Loading only creates
# the module's context; dmod_init() runs on enable, and so does the pulling in
# of required modules (dmip here). A module left merely loaded therefore never
# registers anything and never answers a packet - silently, since nothing it
# imports has been bound yet, so nothing crashes either.

module load dmicmp
module enable dmicmp
exit $?
